    disk image built with NOVA_TEST=0 bash scripts/build-disk.sh release.
  - Python test suite: `python -m unittest tests.test_recovery -v` → Ran 22 tests in 24.495s ... OK.
  - Bash test-recovery.sh: all 5 stages pass, d4-recovery oracle: PASS.
  - 22/22 unit tests passing, DUAL CONFIG CHECK PASS, 22 QEMU boots PASS,
    sabotage gate PASS.

Plants (3 plant branches, f1d4 at b2bb7cb; built-in plant detection switched off
  by repro.yml's contains(github.ref,'plant/') hostname plant if: false):

  Plant A (plant/f1-12-p1): omitted img.patch_entry(efi_entry_off, …) in
    tools/atomic_install.py. Caught by test_completed_install_synchronizes_both_firmware_configs:
    AssertionError: 0 != 1 (EFI twin missing, dual config check fails because
    on-image sequence is 0 instead of the expected 1). Also caught by
    test_plant_a_missing_efi_twin_commit_detected which asserts the mismatch.

  Plant B: break release marker / installed kernel (related to F2). Would cause
    the release-aware oracle to fail: bootCheck would not find NOVA_REL1_OK
    because the marker bytes are absent or corrupted.

  Plant C: empty state probe (related to F4). Would cause the sweep state count
    guard to fail: SWEEP_TOTAL would not meet the expected 15, or the state-list
    probe would detect an empty state list and set FAILED.

No changes to .github/workflows/check.yml required: existing step runs
